
  <sn><md>### Inceptisols {.text-center .fg-red}

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-md-9
**Concept:**

Latin word ‘inceptum’ means ++beginning++. So Inceptisols means the `soils that just started to develop`. They are `embryonic soils` with few diagnostic features. They are `immature soils` having profile features more weakly expressed than matured soils but `show more development than Entisols`. They retain `close resemblances to the parent material`.
:::

